@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: first-phase pawn gas and occupying the square are ONE action, so the extra CC is not spent
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no pawn, gas, CC, or phase types exist under
'   the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning engine
'   module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the collision this must not break _spec/_plans/tutorial-pawn-gas-collision.puml
'   the animation that must not gate it _spec/_plans/deploy-death-animation-layers.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "allow pawn 1st phase gas + move onto square (saves CC)" is a RULES change,
' not a tutorial beat and not a sprite. Three claims are already in the sentence:
'   FIRST PHASE   gas is legal in phase 1 of the pawn's activation
'   PLUS MOVE     occupying the target square is the same action, not a follow-up
'   SAVES CC      today's split spends an extra CC; joining them is the value
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Guessing any of these is how a wrong legal move ships:
'   what gas does to the square and to units standing on it
'   whether occupying is optional or required once gas is declared
'   whether the saved CC is the activation tax or a second action point
'   friendly fire — the collision tutorial names ally tank vs mecha, so gas
'     already has a collision story this rule must not contradict
'
' CC is left as the token the backlog used. Expanding it to a type name before
' the owning module is found invents a vocabulary the engine may not share.
title PLANNED — first-phase pawn gas occupies the square;\nthe saved CC is the whole value

component "phase 1 of the pawn" as P1 <<app>>
component "gas on the square" as GAS <<app>>
component "occupy the square" as OCC <<app>>
component "**two CC spent**\ngas, then a second move" as TAX <<error>>
component "one action, one CC" as JOIN <<app>>
component "collision with an ally\ntank vs mecha" as HIT <<error>>

P1 ARROW_MAIN GAS
GAS ARROW_ERROR TAX : today, a second spend
OCC ARROW_ERROR TAX
GAS ARROW_OPTIONAL JOIN : what this plan allows
OCC ARROW_OPTIONAL JOIN
JOIN ARROW_ERROR HIT : legal gas can still\nstrike a friend

note bottom of TAX
  **Gas and occupying are billed as separate
  activations, so an extra command counter is
  spent for a single intent.** Joining that
  activation recovers the wasted counter and later
  phases remain unchanged until a test names them.
end note

note bottom of JOIN
  **Occupying the square belongs to first-phase
  gas rather than a sequel activation.** Phase one
  may vent and stand without a second counter,
  leaving later phases unchanged until a
  measurement requires otherwise.
end note

note bottom of HIT
  **Friendly fire remains a separate collision
  rule from the joined activation.** The tutorial
  names an allied tank versus a mecha, so this
  join must not quietly cancel that collision.
end note

note right of GAS
  **Gas payload remains unspecified in the backlog
  item and must not be invented during planning.**
  Measure its effect on tiles and units in the
  owning module before any covers line can be
  honest.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Find the cost table.** Name the type that spends CC, the phase gate on
  pawn gas, and the move-onto-square action as they exist today. Until those
  three are real symbols, this plan has no honest covers: line.
  --
  **2. Make the join the legal form.** One activation: phase-1 gas may occupy
  the target square and spend one CC. Keep the split illegal, or keep it as a
  more expensive option — pick one and test both.
  ==
  **3. Freeze collision before teaching it.** Ally tank vs mecha is
  tutorial-pawn-gas-collision.puml. If the join changes who is hit, the
  tutorial is teaching a lie.
  --
  **Left open**: the name behind CC; whether occupy is mandatory after gas;
  whether a pawn already on the square still pays.
end legend
@enduml
